# Rank 1747 / CVE-2020-6164: Silverstripe framework shipped four
# default top-level routes in _config/routes.yml (`interactive`,
# `InstallerTest//$Action/$ID/$OtherID`, `SapphireInfo//...`,
# `SapphireREPL//...`), reachable unauthenticated over the web. Hitting
# /interactive ran SapphireREPL::index(), whose non-CLI branch returns
# "The SilverStripe Interactive Command-line doesn't work in a web
# browser. Use 'sake interactive'..." -- the response itself is the
# payload, disclosing that the domain runs Silverstripe (CWE-200;
# GHSA-gm5x-hpmw-xpxg: "no disclosure of the specific version"; the
# REPL's eval loop is "limited to execution in a CLI context, and is
# not known to present a vulnerability through web-based access").
# Pool SHA 91d30db88f resolves only in silverstripe/silverstripe-
# framework and names this CVE in its message; the cms clone carries
# all 7047 commits and no such object (GitHub "not our ref"), and the
# advisory lists framework among the affected packages with its own
# patched versions (4.4.7, 4.5.4) -- the repo! flag is the multi-
# repository-advisory case, not a mislink. The fixed revision removes the four
# route registrations and deletes SapphireREPL.php; InstallerTest.php
# and SapphireInfo.php survive byte-identical except an added
# @deprecated docblock. Remediation verified present at the fixed revision.
#
# ATTENTION, authorization decided by wiring/configuration, the family
# of ranks 1514, 1535, 1540, 1556, 1557 and 1593. The defect is a YAML
# route registration plus a static response string; there is no dataflow
# for a scanner to follow, and the remediation lives in a file no PHP
# frontend reads. Measured on both revisions (three --cache off runs per
# side, stable): 919 findings at the parent, 916 at the fixed revision; the only
# rows touching these controllers are three VYQL-INJ-004 HtmlRender hits
# on the REPL's `echo CLI::text(...)` colour lines (63/64/98), sourced
# by cross-file library-param taint from FileField.php:175 through
# MarkedSet.getSubtreeAsArray into CLI.text -- param-source noise on
# both sides of nothing relevant, gone at the fixed revision only because the whole
# file is deleted. The sink half works: `vyql match` labels
# `eval($command)` at SapphireREPL.php:92 code.CodeEval (php.sinks@
# resolved), and the source list is empty -- nothing treats fgets(STDIN)
# as untrusted. Two candidate bindings are measured and not shipped.
# A STDIN source: 72 PHP files across the sibling clones read STDIN and
# two co-occur with eval, both MediaWiki maintenance REPLs
# (maintenance/eval.php, benchmarks/benchmarkEval.php) -- by-design CLI
# evaluators identical in kind to SapphireREPL, and flagging them
# contradicts the advisory's own scoping of the weakness to the web
# route. An allowed_actions gate: SilverStripe documents the
# `'action' => 'ADMIN'` permission form, but 22 framework classes use
# the bare-name form, all of them authorizing elsewhere (init(),
# extensions, not being routed), and InstallerTest is byte-identical at
# both revisions, so the binding cannot separate them and fires on 20+
# legitimate internals (the measured identical-on-both-revisions family
# of 1331). The 1380 counterweight fails: the fixed revision deletes the guarded
# method rather than leaving an API call inside it. Disclosure concepts
# considered and rejected: code.ErrorDetailDisclosure, code.Absolute-
# PathDisclosure, code.VerboseHttpErrorObjectDisclosure -- none covers a
# static product-identity string, and "controller action returns a
# literal" fires on ordinary content actions at both revisions.
#
# Spec cve_rank1747 pins the miss against the rules of the right
# classes that exist today: the REPL's eval loop against VYQL-INJ-003
# (the sink is labelled; the member must flip to expect only if
# console input ever becomes core.UserControlledData, which the
# precision measurement above argues against), and the routed
# disclosure actions against VYQL-SEC-004. The guarded member is
# SapphireInfo's own ADMIN gate, drawn from the same tree at both
# revisions, and must stay reject under all of them.

test "rank1747: the routed repl controller evals console input and answers web requests with product-identifying text"
  lang php
  file src/Dev/SapphireREPL.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace SilverStripe\Dev;

  use SilverStripe\Control\Controller;
  use SilverStripe\Control\Director;

  class SapphireREPL extends Controller
  {
      private static $allowed_actions = array(
          'index'
      );

      public function index()
      {
          if (!Director::is_cli()) {
              return "The SilverStripe Interactive Command-line doesn't work in a web browser."
                  . " Use 'sake interactive' from the command-line to run.";
          }

          while (true) {
              $command = trim(fgets(STDIN, 4096));

              if ($command == 'quit' || $command == '\q') {
                  break ;
              }

              if (substr($command, -1) == ';') {
                  $command = substr($command, 0, -1);
              }
              $is_print = preg_match('/^\s*print/i', $command);
              if (!$is_print) {
                  $command = "return ($command)";
              }
              $command .= ";";

              $result = eval($command);
              print_r($result);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

